IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-art03-commencement: Article 3 of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021), Commencement of Jersey legislation.
--
-- THIS MODULE IS MEANT TO BE COPIED BY HAND into another encoding (the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014's).
-- It imports only prelude, daydate and je21-nouns, and every function in it is self-contained:
-- no function calls another function of this module, so a copier takes the ones they want, with the nouns named in the comment above each.
-- The nouns come from je21-nouns.l4: `Time of day`, `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)`, `Moment of coming into force`,
-- `Reading L1 of the day after a silent provision is made`, `Reading L2 of a stated time of day`, `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`,
-- `Reading L12 of an applicability clause`.
-- A copy should carry a comment citing this subject (legislation-2021, row legalese-2026-10) and the Article.
--
-- The seat is the reader of an enactment who asks when a provision bound them.
-- The unit of an answer is a MOMENT: a day, and what Article 3 says about the time of day on it.
-- A question about a DAY ("was it in force at some time on that day?") never needs the time of day.
-- A question about a TIME OF DAY on a day is answered where the Law answers it, and refused where it does not.
--
-- The only date arithmetic in the deposit is here: "the day after it is made" (Article 3(1)(b)) is the day made PLUS 1.
-- That is the Law's own step of one calendar day, taken with the DATE type's arithmetic, and no other period is counted anywhere.
--
-- What Article 3 does not say, and what this module does about it (NOTES.md sections 6 and 7):
--   L1  the time of day at which a silent provision comes into force on the day after it is made (default: refuse a question about a time of day on that day);
--   L2  whether a stated time of day is "provision to the contrary" to the beginning-of-day rule of Article 3(2) (default: it is);
--   L3  the time at which Part 2 itself came into force on 28 September 2021, which matters to Article 3(6) (default: the beginning of that day, by Article 3(2)).

§ `Article 3 -- Commencement of Jersey legislation`

§§ `3(1) A provision that is silent as to its commencement`

-- Needs: `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)`, `Time of day`, `Moment of coming into force`, `Reading L1 of the day after a silent provision is made`.
-- Answers: when does a provision of legislation that says nothing about its commencement come into force?
-- (a) legislation having effect only to commence other legislation, or an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2): when it is made.
-- (b) any other legislation: on the day after it is made.
-- For (a) the moment is the time of making on the day made, if the caller knows it.
-- src:45 | (1) If Jersey legislation is silent as to the commencement of any of its provisions that provision comes into force –
-- src:46 | (a) in the case of legislation having effect only to commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2), when it is made; and
-- src:47 | (b) in the case of any other legislation, on the day after it is made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(1) (src:45-47)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)`
      `the day on which the legislation was made` IS A DATE
      `the time of day at which it was made, if known` IS A MAYBE `Time of day`
      reading IS A `Reading L1 of the day after a silent provision is made`
GIVETH A `Moment of coming into force`
`Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` kind `the day on which the legislation was made` `the time of day at which it was made, if known` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation`
        THEN `from the time it was made on the day` `the day on which the legislation was made` `the time of day at which it was made, if known`
    WHEN `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)`
        THEN `from the time it was made on the day` `the day on which the legislation was made` `the time of day at which it was made, if known`
    WHEN `any other legislation`
        THEN CONSIDER reading
            WHEN `the Law does not say at what time of that day, so a question about a time of day on it is refused`
                THEN `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` (`the day on which the legislation was made` PLUS 1)
            WHEN `the provision is in force from the beginning of that day`
                THEN `from the beginning of the day` (`the day on which the legislation was made` PLUS 1)

§§ `3(2) Legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day`

-- Needs: `Time of day`, `Moment of coming into force`, `Reading L2 of a stated time of day`.
-- Answers: when does legislation that is expressed to come into force on a particular day come into force?
-- At the beginning of that day, "unless provision is made to the contrary".
-- A stated time of day is the one thing the Law does not say is such a provision: fork L2, default that it is.
-- src:48 | (2) If any Jersey legislation is expressed to come into force on a particular day, it is treated as coming into force at the beginning of that day, unless provision is made to the contrary.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(2) (src:48)
GIVEN `the day the legislation names` IS A DATE
      `the time of day the legislation states for it, if any` IS A MAYBE `Time of day`
      reading IS A `Reading L2 of a stated time of day`
GIVETH A `Moment of coming into force`
`Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` `the day the legislation names` `the time of day the legislation states for it, if any` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time of day the legislation states for it, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `from the beginning of the day` `the day the legislation names`
    WHEN JUST stated
        THEN CONSIDER reading
            WHEN `a stated time of day is provision to the contrary, and the legislation comes into force at that time`
                THEN `from a stated time on the day` `the day the legislation names` stated
            WHEN `a stated time of day does not displace the beginning of the day`
                THEN `from the beginning of the day` `the day the legislation names`

§§ `Reading a moment: a day, and a time of day on it`

-- Needs: `Moment of coming into force`.
-- Answers: was the provision in force at some time on the day asked about?
-- It was if the day asked about is the day it came into force or a later one, whatever the Law says about the time of day.
-- src:45 | (1) If Jersey legislation is silent as to the commencement of any of its provisions that provision comes into force –
-- src:46 | (a) in the case of legislation having effect only to commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2), when it is made; and
-- src:47 | (b) in the case of any other legislation, on the day after it is made.
-- src:48 | (2) If any Jersey legislation is expressed to come into force on a particular day, it is treated as coming into force at the beginning of that day, unless provision is made to the contrary.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(1) and (2) (src:45-48)
GIVEN moment IS A `Moment of coming into force`
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` moment `the day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER moment
    WHEN `from the beginning of the day` first THEN `the day asked about` AT LEAST first
    WHEN `from a stated time on the day` first stated THEN `the day asked about` AT LEAST first
    WHEN `from the time it was made on the day` first made THEN `the day asked about` AT LEAST first
    WHEN `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` first THEN `the day asked about` AT LEAST first

-- Needs: `Moment of coming into force`, `Time of day`.
-- Answers: was the provision in force at a given time of day on a given day?
-- Before the day it came into force: no.
-- After it: yes.
-- On it: from the beginning of the day, yes; from a stated time, from that time; from the time it was made, from that time if the caller knows it.
-- Where the Law does not say at what time of the day the provision came into force, or the time of making is not known, the model refuses.
-- src:45 | (1) If Jersey legislation is silent as to the commencement of any of its provisions that provision comes into force –
-- src:46 | (a) in the case of legislation having effect only to commence other legislation or consisting of an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2), when it is made; and
-- src:47 | (b) in the case of any other legislation, on the day after it is made.
-- src:48 | (2) If any Jersey legislation is expressed to come into force on a particular day, it is treated as coming into force at the beginning of that day, unless provision is made to the contrary.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(1) and (2) (src:45-48)
GIVEN moment IS A `Moment of coming into force`
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the time of day asked about` IS A `Time of day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` moment `the day asked about` `the time of day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER moment
    WHEN `from the beginning of the day` first THEN `the day asked about` AT LEAST first
    WHEN `from a stated time on the day` first stated
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN first THEN FALSE
                IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN first THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE
                        (`the time of day asked about`'s `hour of the day` TIMES 60 PLUS `the time of day asked about`'s `minute of the hour`)
                    AT LEAST (stated's `hour of the day` TIMES 60 PLUS stated's `minute of the hour`)
    WHEN `from the time it was made on the day` first made
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN first THEN FALSE
                IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN first THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE
                    CONSIDER made
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "the time of day at which the legislation was made is not given, so whether it was in force at a time of day on the day it was made cannot be answered"
                    WHEN JUST madeAt
                        THEN     (`the time of day asked about`'s `hour of the day` TIMES 60 PLUS `the time of day asked about`'s `minute of the hour`)
                             AT LEAST (madeAt's `hour of the day` TIMES 60 PLUS madeAt's `minute of the hour`)
    WHEN `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` first
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN first THEN FALSE
                IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN first THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE REFUSE "the Law does not say at what time of the day after it is made a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force"

§§ `3(3) Regulations that commence by an Order of a Minister`

-- Answers: does Article 3(3) let Regulations provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister?
-- Only Regulations, and only "unless provision is made to the contrary", which the caller states.
-- FALSE means Article 3(3) does not confer the power; it does not mean the power is unavailable elsewhere.
-- src:49 | (3) Unless provision is made to the contrary, Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(3) (src:49)
GIVEN `the instrument is Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3(3): Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister` `the instrument is Regulations` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
        `the instrument is Regulations`
    AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

§§ `3(4) Different days, times or events for different provisions`

-- Answers: where a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in it,
-- may that power specify different days, times or events for different provisions?
-- Article 3(4) has no "unless" limb.
-- FALSE means the conditions of Article 3(4) are not met.
-- Fork L12: the opening condition names what the paragraph covers, as an applicability clause does.
-- On the reading taken, a power outside it is not covered by the paragraph and the answer is FALSE; on the other the Law does not say whether the paragraph reaches it, and the model refuses.
-- src:50 | (4) If a Law, Regulations made under a Law or any provision of a Law or Regulations may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order, the power may be exercised to specify different days, times or events for different provisions of the Law or Regulations to commence.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(4) (src:50)
GIVEN `it is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      reading IS A `Reading L12 of an applicability clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` `it is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either` `it may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order` reading MEANS
    IF     `it is a Law, Regulations made under a Law, or a provision of either`
       AND `it may be commenced by an Act of the States or an Order of a Minister on a day specified in the Act or Order`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER reading
         WHEN `an applicability clause is exhaustive, so what lies outside it is not within the Article` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `an applicability clause only names what it includes, so the Law does not say whether the Article reaches what lies outside it`
             THEN REFUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether it reaches any other power"

§§ `3(5) Amendment of legislation that has not come into force`

-- Answers: does an amendment of legislation that has not come into force commence the legislation amended?
-- No: Article 3(5)(a).
-- If the amended legislation is already in force, Article 3(5) does not apply and the Law does not say.
-- src:51 | (5) If any Jersey legislation amends any other legislation or provision that has not come into force –
-- src:52 | (a) the amendment of the uncommenced legislation does not commence that legislation or provision; and
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(5)(a) (src:51-52)
GIVEN `the legislation or provision amended has not come into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3(5)(a): the amendment of uncommenced legislation commences the legislation amended` `the legislation or provision amended has not come into force` MEANS
    IF `the legislation or provision amended has not come into force`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 3(5) deals only with an amendment of legislation or a provision that has not come into force"

-- Needs: `Moment of coming into force`.
-- Answers: when does the amendment made by the amending legislation commence?
-- When the provision amended commences, "unless provision is made otherwise" (a fact the caller states, together with the moment that other provision gives).
-- NOTHING means the provision amended has not yet commenced, so neither has the amendment: the source names this absent case.
-- src:51 | (5) If any Jersey legislation amends any other legislation or provision that has not come into force –
-- src:52 | (a) the amendment of the uncommenced legislation does not commence that legislation or provision; and
-- src:53 | (b) the amendment made by the amending legislation commences when the provision amended commences unless provision is made otherwise.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(5)(b) (src:51-53)
GIVEN `the moment at which the provision amended comes into force, if it has` IS A MAYBE `Moment of coming into force`
      `provision is made otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment that other provision gives, if any` IS A MAYBE `Moment of coming into force`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment of coming into force`
`Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences` `the moment at which the provision amended comes into force, if it has` `provision is made otherwise` `the moment that other provision gives, if any` MEANS
    IF `provision is made otherwise`
    THEN CONSIDER `the moment that other provision gives, if any`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "provision is made otherwise, and the moment it gives is not supplied"
         WHEN JUST given THEN JUST given
    ELSE `the moment at which the provision amended comes into force, if it has`

§§ `3(6) Legislation that had commenced before Part 2 did`

-- Needs: `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`.
-- Answers: does Article 3 govern when this legislation commenced?
-- It does not for legislation that "had commenced before the commencement of this Part", and Part 2 came into force on 28 September 2021 (endnotes, Table of Legislation History).
-- The caller gives the day on which the legislation (or provision) commenced, under whatever rule applied, or nothing if it has not commenced.
-- Not commenced: Article 3 governs.
-- Commenced on or before 27 September 2021: it commenced before Part 2 did, so Article 3 does not affect it.
-- Commenced after 28 September 2021: Article 3 governs.
-- Commenced ON 28 September 2021: whether that is "before" depends on the time of day at which Part 2 came into force that day, fork L3.
-- src:54 | (6) Nothing in this Article affects the commencement of any Jersey legislation that had commenced before the commencement of this Part.
-- src:258 | (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:259 | L.8/2021
-- src:260 | 28
-- src:261 | September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3(6) and the endnotes' Table of Legislation History (src:54, src:258-261)
GIVEN `the day on which the legislation commenced, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      reading IS A `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` `the day on which the legislation commenced, if it has` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the legislation commenced, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST commenced
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF commenced LESS THAN YMD 2021 9 28 THEN FALSE
                IF commenced GREATER THAN YMD 2021 9 28 THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE
                    CONSIDER reading
                    WHEN `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)` THEN TRUE
                    WHEN `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
                        THEN REFUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 2 of the Law came into force, so whether legislation that commenced that day commenced before it cannot be answered"
